###  http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#overallintent_instance
:overallintent_instance rdf:type :OverallIntent ;
                rdfs:label "the overallintent"@en ;
                rdfs:comment "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Propaganda; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes two images: the top image shows two men kissing in a dimly lit, possibly club-like setting, while the bottom image shows two women in wedding attire kissing affectionately. The text 'love is love' is overlaid. The overall intent is to promote the message of LGBTQ+ acceptance and equality by equating the romantic and marital expressions of love between same-sex couples with those of heterosexual couples. This is a form of propaganda aimed at influencing public opinion toward greater acceptance of same-sex relationships and marriage. The meme does not contain any toxic elements such as abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or ableist content. It is a positive, affirming message intended to normalize and celebrate diverse expressions of love."@en ;
                :extractionMethod "llm_extraction_huggingface" ;
                :extractedFrom "36058.png" ;
                :extractionTimestamp "2025-12-15T23:15:26.358646" .

